msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_1"
msgstr ""
"It's craftier than anything we've come up against. And it has one trick that"
" there's still no way to counter."

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_10"
msgstr ""
"The Ferryman led Alex to the Tower knowing that she would hate it. He's a "
"manipulator, but not suicidal. That means he had a plan. We have to find out"
" what it was."

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_11"
msgstr ""
"I never had a home. Now I do. And I've just realized what I'm prepared to do"
" to keep it."

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_12"
msgstr "It works! The frequency is blocked! Fire, Smith! Destroy it!"

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_13"
msgstr ""
"We did it. The Spider is no more. The Tower has been destroyed. Now we need "
"to decide Alex’s fate. Every one of us has to make a choice."

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_2"
msgstr ""
"Repair docks, private cabins, the smell of hot coffee in the cafeteria. A "
"cozy home amid this damned anomaly. But one thought worries me..."

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_3"
msgstr ""
"I have a plan and a tank almost ready to execute it. There's just one piece "
"missing. And only you can help with that."

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_4"
msgstr ""
"You've come to destroy the Tower. Destroy my home. You call it a danger, but"
" that's a lie. You just want power."

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_5"
msgstr ""
"We weren't saving the world. We were doing what the Ferryman needed us to. "
"He was playing us like pawns. Manipulating our every move. And I brought "
"Alex right into his trap."

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_6"
msgstr ""
"The Mirium inside me pulses and leads me deep into the Tower. Answers await "
"me there. The one who called me awaits me there..."

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_7"
msgstr ""
"The Ferryman wasn't looking for the Dark Tower's coordinates. He knew them. "
"He needed all our expeditions for something else. And now it seems I "
"understand what."

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_8"
msgstr ""
"Father gave me a name. Gretchen von Eckhardt. He called me \"pearl.\" I was "
"special."

msgid "meta/shortStory/hw_artefact_9"
msgstr ""
"Those born here are capable of more. We can shape Mirium, control it. For "
"the first time in my life, I feel complete."

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_1"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}It's craftier than anything we've come up against. And it has one trick that there's still no way to counter.{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"Damn it! Why are things never easy? Plan A failed. It was beautiful, spectacular, but it failed.\n"
"\n"
"Everyone thought the {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}Marduk{{/}} was our ace in the hole. A huge flying ship with guns bigger than the Dora's cannon.\n"
"\n"
"One salvo, and all our problems would be solved. {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}The Dark Tower{{/}} destroyed; the Nazis, or what was left of them, neutralized. And all those thousands of tanks that they'd prepared for attack back in the '40s would stay here to rust forever.\n"
"\n"
"But I forgot rule number one: in the anomaly, things are never easy. The shells got stuck in that damned shield. And to take it out, we'd need to destroy the thing that generates it.\n"
"\n"
"But that {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}Spider{{/}} is craftier than anything we've come up against. First you need to get to it. And then, when all that's left is to deliver the final blow, it activates the damned Magnus and retreats to its lair to lick its wounds. And hurls us a few phases back.\n"
"\n"
"Alright, enough waxing lyrical. It's time for action. Either we deactivate that shield and blow the Tower to hell, or we'll stay here forever.\n"
"\n"
"The command built its huge ship, even gave it the name of a god and thought the problem was solved. But in the end, here we are again. Gods fail us. Tanks don't.\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"Use the tactical map and coordinate your actions. Mark the point you are heading to so that the platoon moves with you. Or proceed to a position chosen by another commander. Always stick together.\"{{/}}"

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_10"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}The Ferryman led Alex to the Tower knowing that she would hate it. He's a manipulator, but not suicidal. That means he had a plan. We have to find out what it was.{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"We're in a trap. In her web. Alex is learning. It doesn't matter if we win or lose—with each battle, she grows stronger. It seems she's just playing with us, testing what the Spider can do.\n"
"\n"
"I can't stop thinking that everything is playing out according to the Ferryman's script. But I can't understand his logic. He's a manipulator, but not suicidal. He led her to the Tower knowing that she would hate it. How did he plan to control her?\n"
"\n"
"In any case, it's too late. Smith keeps hoping he can talk to her and bring her round. He wants to save her. I'd like to as well, but that's not Alex anymore.\n"
"\n"
"I read the German archives. They tried to extract the operators. Seventeen attempts. Four survived, but none of them returned to consciousness. They breathed, their hearts beat, but no one was home. And yet... Alex is no ordinary operator.\n"
"\n"
"Enough. We don't have time for this. We need to destroy the Dark Tower. \n"
"\n"
"The Sharur, I mean, the Eclipse, is ready. I'm loading it with {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}superdense Mirium{{/}} now. We only have one shot, and we have to be sure we've found the right frequency.\n"
"\n"
"Bring in the last type of echo tank, and we'll be ready. Once we activate the \"{{@ class $keyWordViolet}}jammer{{/}},\" we'll have a thirty second opening. The Spider will stop receiving the signal from the Tower and won't be able to escape. That's our only chance to deliver the deciding blow. \n"
"\n"
"Bring the final specimen.\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"Within the Anomaly, unique mechanics changes the rules. Pay attention to the notification displayed at the beginning of the third phase. Some mechanics force you move faster, others demand tactics and attentiveness.\"{{/}}"

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_11"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}I never had a home. Now I do. And I've just realized what I'm prepared to do to keep it.{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"I sense it. Mirium. It's not evil. Not lonely. It's not anything. It doesn't think, it just exists. It merges with the host and strengthens them, if they can handle it.\n"
"\n"
"But is it possible to free yourself completely from your body? To {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}merge with Mirium{{/}}? To become a part of it. That could save me.\n"
"\n"
"The soldiers want to destroy the Dark Tower. And me? Smith is constantly trying to speak to me. He insists he wants to save me. But can he be believed? What if he's just part of another one of the Ferryman's manipulations?  \n"
"\n"
"The Ferryman. This is all because of him. He wants power. He wants to seize the technology. To seize me. And the soldiers are helping him do it, even if they don't realize it themselves. \n"
"\n"
"They're already close. I need more time. I've finally become complete. My whole life, I never had a home, now I do. I just realized what I'm prepared to do to keep it. \n"
"\n"
"You're all in on this. But I won't be your puppet again!\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"If you have Energy Shield, use it only as a last resort—if your hit points are low or before an encounter with a Hedgehog.\"{{/}}"

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_12"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}It works! The frequency is blocked! Fire, Smith! Destroy it!{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"MOREL: It's damaged enough! Smith, the Spider is preparing to jump! I'm turning on the jammer... Yes! It's working! The frequency is blocked! Fire, Smith! Destroy it!\n"
"\n"
"SMITH: ...\n"
"\n"
"MOREL: Smith?! Fire! Come on!\n"
"\n"
"SMITH: Damn... Alex is still there, in the Tower. If I destroy the Spider, she'll die too. We have to save her... at least try!\n"
"\n"
"MOREL: Smith, damn you! It's either her or all of us!\n"
"\n"
"SMITH: We can't do that. There has to be another way. We've got to get her out of there! I can't!\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"Pay attention to the tactical map and how the damage zone changes during the boss fight. As soon as the boss tries to escape, pursue it while staying in the safe zone. Once outside the safe zone, use Turbocharger to avoid damage to your vehicle.\"{{/}}"

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_13"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}We did it. The Spider is no more. The Tower has been destroyed. Now we need to decide Alex’s fate. Every one of us has to make a choice.{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"She did it! Alex. At the last moment, she took {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}the form of pure Mirium{{/}} and destroyed the Spider. The shield was disabled. The Marduk's shells hit their mark. The upper levels of the Tower are destroyed, but the lower levels survived, and we registered a signal inside. Weak, but stable. It's Alex. The Mirium is keeping her alive for now.\n"
"\n"
"We descended. We found the cocoon with her body and her last notes. She made a choice. Alex destroyed the Spider to destroy the Tower together with her human shell and finally merge with Mirium.\n"
"\n"
"Smith doesn't believe it was her conscious choice. He's convinced that the Mirium simply clouded her judgment. He recalls that in the notes, she admitted she couldn't always control her own thoughts. The captain intends to take her body and connect it into the ship's systems. He wants to preserve her at any cost, find a way to free her from the Mirium and return her to consciousness. Make her into a normal person again.\n"
"\n"
"Alex wrote that she felt at home for the first time. She didn't destroy the Spider under our orders. She decided to do it herself. Her home isn't this Tower. Her home is Mirium.\n"
"\n"
"If we destroy the Tower, Alex will be reborn. She'll merge with the matter not as an ordinary operator, but as something entirely new.\n"
"\n"
"That affects us all. Everyone who fought at this Tower. Decide."

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_2"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}Repair docks, private cabins, the smell of hot coffee in the cafeteria. A cozy home amid this damned anomaly. But one thought worries me...{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"Damn, that was close. I had the Spider in my sights. I was milliseconds short.\n"
"\n"
"I'll never get used to the Marduk. Before, when we were at our base in Babylon, every trip into the anomaly was a leap into the abyss. We \"resurfaced\" exhausted, deflated, and as if we were strangers. But now we have this ship. The Marduk...\n"
"\n"
"It has built-in Magnuses, and now we can \"jump\" to almost any phase. We just need an exact route. {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}Morel{{/}}, our chief engineer, says Mirium isn't just layers placed one on top of the other. It's more like a network of patterns, connected by complex pathways. {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}A maze{{/}}. And if there's no map, it's easy to get lost in it and stay there forever. To eternally roam through the phases and not know whether you're getting closer to home or further away.\n"
"\n"
"But now we're where we're supposed to be. And we have everything we need: a huge ship, experienced tankers, and Morel with his new technology. We can now even capture echo tanks and keep them in a solid state. Stabilize them and not let them turn back into liquid Mirium. Morel is opening them up, studying them, looking for a way to beat the Spider. And we continue to break through this protective field.\n"
"\n"
"Basically, we've got everything here: repair docks, private cabins, a gym, and even hot coffee in the cafeteria. A cozy little home amid the damned anomaly. I'm starting to get used to the comfort, and it worries me. The terror surrounding us is becoming the norm. We have to finish off this damned Tower faster and get back to our real home.\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"Do not attempt to destroy the Immortal. Do not waste your time and ammo. Do not stand still. Move, and do not let yourself get cornered.\"{{/}}"

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_3"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}I have a plan and a tank almost ready to execute it. There's just one piece missing. And only you can help with that.{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"One second, one second... Okay we need to stabilize {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}the stasis field{{/}}; otherwise, that thing will turn to liquid Mirium right here in my workshop.\n"
"\n"
"Now I can introduce myself. Pleased to meet you. {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}Jacques Morel{{/}}. Thanks for bringing in this specimen whole. Usually I'm only given fragments and vessels of liquid Mirium. But this we can work with.\n"
"\n"
"I have an idea. The echo tanks are controlled from the Dark Tower. That's a fact. They're like puppets on invisible strings. The Spider is too. Hmm...a damned interesting machine. Why did they choose this kind of platform? It's clearly connected to gravity somehow...\n"
"\n"
"Sorry, I got distracted. To catch the Spider and not let it get away, we need to cut those strings. Jam the signal. But there are a lot of strings. Each one on its own frequency. Now my sensors are picking up a whole choir on different wavelengths. If you bring me echo tank specimens of each type, I'll study their frequencies, filter them out, and we'll find out on which exact frequency the Spider receives its orders.\n"
"\n"
"And then the Sharur will come into play. A symbol of divine power and intellect prevailing over chaos. Like the legendary mace of Ninurta, it will crush our opponents. Don't memorize all these names. It's just a tribute to tradition—everything here is named in honor of Sumerian mythology. In the documentation I'll put things plainer: {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}Eclipse{{/}}. A heavily armored tank that can get close to the Spider and jam its signal. It just needs to be finished and set to the right frequency. We simply have to collect all types of echo tanks.\n"
"\n"
"I'd do it myself, but... Okay, who am I kidding? I couldn't manage without you.\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"Always stick together. Remember: when you break away from the platoon and go to another point alone, you provoke the echo tanks. Once your vehicle is destroyed, they will start attacking your allies from behind. Do not jeopardize your mission.\"{{/}}"

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_4"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}You've come to destroy the Tower. Destroy my home. You call it a danger, but that's a lie. You just want power.{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"Leave. You don't belong here.\n"
"\n"
"The clatter of your tracks... Before, that sound would mean salvation, now... Now you've come to destroy the Tower. Destroy my home. You call it a danger, but that's a lie. You just want power. You want to possess that which you cannot understand. You want to control Mirium, turn it into a weapon, and make me into your obedient plaything.\n"
"\n"
"The ones who came before you also tried to control it. They built, captured, possessed, but in the end they lost themselves.\n"
"\n"
"Clear off! You know nothing. You understand nothing. You're all puppets in HIS hands. {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}The Ferryman{{/}} is simply playing with us all. We're no one to him.\n"
"\n"
"And now he's directed you to my home. He wants me destroyed. But you're too late. I don't need saving anymore. Now I can take care of myself.\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"Do not only rely on your tank's armor. Seek cover and hide your vulnerable areas. It's trite advice, but many do forget about it in the anomaly. Perhaps due to how Mirium affects our minds.\"{{/}}"

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_5"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}We weren't saving the world. We were doing what the Ferryman needed us to. He was playing us like pawns. Manipulating our every move. And I brought Alex right into his trap.{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"Damn it... That voice I hear over the radio. It's her. {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}Alex{{/}}. The photographer who entered the Forbidden Zone. She discovered the source of the attack, transmitted us the recordings, asked us to take her. She waited for me to come for her, but I... I followed orders. \"The priority is to suppress the threats.\" \"Evacuation is inexpedient.\" I left her there. Alone.\n"
"\n"
"Morel confirmed my worst fears. The Ferryman, that son of a bitch from the security office, planned the whole thing. He knew she was the daughter of the same general who commanded that Tower. {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}Gretchen von Eckhardt{{/}}. It's her childhood voice that remained in the echo that we heard in the anomaly. \n"
"\n"
"We weren't saving the world. We were doing what the Ferryman needed us to. He was playing us like pawns. Manipulating our every move. And I brought Alex right into his trap.\n"
"\n"
"Morel says she's no longer human. That the Mirium has taken hold of her and it's irreversible. But the Lost don't talk like that. She didn't lose consciousness. She's still here. Alone.\n"
"\n"
"I have to save her. I just have to.\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"Mark the vehicles you are going to attack to coordinate fire and prompt your allies to focus on one enemy. Amass a local firepower advantage.\"{{/}}"

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_6"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}The Mirium inside me pulses and leads me deep into the Tower. Answers await me there. The one who called me awaits me there...{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"[Seven days until the assault]\n"
"\n"
"A recording... but I don't know which. How much time has passed since entering the anomaly—I don't know either. The teleporter didn't take me to Babylon. I ended up in the Dark Tower. \n"
"\n"
"The Mirium inside me pulses, takes over my thoughts, leads me. It leads me to {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}the control room{{/}}. It seems again that I've been here before. Everything is familiar. These empty {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}cocoons{{/}}. And the one she's inside. Was it her that called me?\n"
"\n"
"Who is she? She looks almost inhuman. Pale skin, only purple Mirium pulses through her veins. Keeps her alive. If you can call it being alive.\n"
"\n"
"She has to know all the answers. She has to explain to me what's going on here. How can I talk to her? Put on the same {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}helmet{{/}}? No. First, while I have the strength, I need to look around the Tower.\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"Keep an eye on the allied vehicles' hit points. If you have Group Repairs, restore hit points to the damaged platoon members. Even one lost vehicle jeopardizes the entire mission.\"{{/}}"

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_7"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}The Ferryman wasn't looking for the Dark Tower's coordinates. He knew them. He needed all our expeditions for something else. And now it seems I understand what.{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"Is that you? Have you heard? The Ferryman has disappeared. He's fled and probably moved on to the next part of his plan. He wasn't looking for the Dark Tower's coordinates. He knew them. All our expeditions, all those losses were needed for something else.\n"
"\n"
"Well, thanks to the specimens you brought in, I've realized why he needed Alex. But the others?\n"
"\n"
"Look: judging by the German archives, there are {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}operators{{/}} in the Dark Tower who send commands to the echo tanks. But a normal human mind can't control thousands of machines simultaneously, so a small group always comes to face us, of fifteen. That's the limit of one operator. The Tower needs new \"minds.\" Fresh, compatible ones.\n"
"\n"
"Alex isn't just some random photographer who got into the anomaly. As we now know, she is Gretchen von Eckhardt, {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}the daughter of the general{{/}} who commanded this Tower.\n"
"\n"
"The name Gretchen comes from the Greek \"Margaret\" and means \"pearl.\" That's no coincidence. That's what her father called her when he saw something special in her. It's likely that she's the one the German archives called the \"Überlenker,\" or {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}super operator{{/}}.\n"
"\n"
"If the thing that Alex became unleashes its potential, if it remembers how to control Mirium, thousands of tanks will gush out of the anomaly at once.\n"
"\n"
"We need to hurry. Time is against us.\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"When fighting the boss, use the special ammo picked up in phases, along with your vehicle's special perks, to deal more damage to the vulnerable spots in your enemy's armor.\"{{/}}"

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_8"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}Father gave me a name. Gretchen von Eckhardt. He called me \"pearl.\" I was special.{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"[Seven days until the assault]\n"
"\n"
"My name is Gretchen.\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $keyWordViolet}}Project Gleipnir{{/}}. The Germans searched for a way to subjugate Mirium. They realized that ordinary people are ineffective and find it difficult to handle even a couple of vehicles. They should have been born here, in the anomaly. Those who are capable of sensing Mirium.\n"
"\n"
"I'm the result of an experiment. We didn't even have names. {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}Biological transmitter{{/}}, object, resource. But to Father, I was special. He left a label on the fields: Gretchen von Eckhardt. He called me \"pearl.\"\n"
"\n"
"The first successful specimen. High capabilities, resilience against Mirium degradation... I'm simply a weapon that was supposed to guide armies of echo tanks through the rifts. Ordinary operators gradually lost their minds, becoming unthinking effectors of another's will. Their consciousness partially passed into the Mirium, the echo. Reaching for it, trying to escape. And when they got out of control, they were simply turned off. Their personalities split, spawning new anomalies in the echo, and their bodies... their bodies still held life, but the people themselves were long gone.\n"
"\n"
"But those were ordinary operators. It says nothing in the documents about those like me. I'm getting weaker. My body won't last long. What if I manage to fully enter the Mirium?\n"
"\n"
"My thoughts are slipping away. Or is the Mirium getting hold of them? I don't know. There are still so many questions.\n"
"\n"
"I have to speak to it. To put on the helmet and learn the whole truth!\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"Turbocharger does not use Mirium to activate. However, it has a cooldown period. Use Turbocharger when absolutely necessary: to get away from the Hedgehog, dodge the Charger, jump out of the Immortal's aura, or dash to Magnus when everyone is ready to teleport.\"{{/}}"

msgid "meta/story/hw_artefact_9"
msgstr ""
"{{@ class $titleClass}}Those born here are capable of more. We can shape Mirium, control it. For the first time in my life, I feel complete.{{/}}\n"
"\n"
"[Seven days until the assault]\n"
"\n"
"It's loud. Too loud. Thousands of signals, noise, whispering. Commands in German—cold, dead orders.   \n"
"\n"
"Can you hear me? Are you here?\n"
"\n"
"There's nothing left of her. This woman in the cocoon, she's just {{@ class $keyWordViolet}}a transmitter{{/}} now. Is that really what my future holds, too? Becoming an echo of old commands?\n"
"\n"
"No. In the documents it says that those born here are capable of more. We can resist the influence of Mirium, control it, shape it.\n"
"\n"
"I need to try. Imagine the particles gathering together.\n"
"\n"
"I feel something. This is strange. Scary. But for the first time I feel complete. I sense that I finally have power.\n"
"\n"
"{{@ class $titleManual}}From the manual:{{/}}\n"
"{{@ class $textManual}}\"Remember: when moving to a new phase, the Anomaly affects the crew and you receive enhancements. Study them and change your tactics with the new options in mind.\"{{/}}"

